# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and in working trees on
# every platform. Git auto-detects text vs binary (`text=auto`), so binary
# files are left untouched. This pins the repo to LF regardless of the
# committer's platform or local core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Rationale: commit e2be6da rewrote ~150 pre-existing files LF->CRLF, which
# made 72% of PR #3's diff line-ending noise and breaks unpinned
# `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebangs. Downstream branches authored against the
# CRLF content should rebase with `git rebase -X renormalize` (and
# `git config merge.renormalize true`).
* text=auto eol=lf

